From: Alaxendol <alecjakopin@mailbox.org>
Subject: [PATCH] rpmsg: glink: refuse reopen while a local close is pending

ModemManager opens and closes the rpmsg_wwan_ctrl AT ports (DATA1, DATA4)
several times within a millisecond at boot. Every open of the
remote-initiated channel goes through qcom_glink_create_remote(), which
allocates a new lcid (and takes a reference) for the same channel while
the previous close is still waiting for its close-ack, and channel->lcid
only remembers the latest one. Trace on OnePlus 12 (SM8650), DATA4 gets
lcids 2, 4, 6, 8 before the first close-ack arrives.

qcom_glink_rx_close_ack() then removes channel->lcid (8) instead of the
acked id (2), sets lcid to 0 and removes the rpmsg device, whose
endpoint destroy sends a close for lcid 0. The later acks put further
references, the ack for 8 hits "close ack on unknown channel", and
lcids 2/4/6 stay in the idr pointing at a channel with a single
reference. qcom_glink_native_remove() puts each of them at modem
shutdown: refcount underflow / use-after-free, an oops in rmtfs, and
with oops=panic a hang at every reboot.

- qcom_glink_create_remote(): return -EBUSY while the channel still owns
  an lcid (open, or close not yet acked).
- qcom_glink_destroy_ept(): don't send a close without a local open.
- qcom_glink_rx_close_ack(): remove the acked lcid, and clear
  channel->lcid only if it is that one.

AI-assisted (Claude).

Upstream-Status: Pending [not submitted; drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_native.c
  is unchanged from mainline here, so this is a candidate for
  linux-remoteproc once tested]

--- a/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_native.c
+++ b/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_native.c
@@ -1290,6 +1290,17 @@
 {
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * A local open (or a close still waiting for its close-ack) already
+	 * owns an lcid for this channel. Opening again would register a
+	 * second lcid for the same channel while channel->lcid only tracks
+	 * the latest one; the close-acks then remove the wrong ids and the
+	 * stale ones are put again in qcom_glink_native_remove() (refcount
+	 * underflow / use-after-free). Refuse until the previous close-ack.
+	 */
+	if (channel->lcid)
+		return -EBUSY;
+
 	qcom_glink_send_open_ack(glink, channel);
 
 	ret = qcom_glink_send_open_req(glink, channel);
@@ -1417,6 +1428,15 @@
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&channel->recv_lock, flags);
 	channel->ept.cb = NULL;
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&channel->recv_lock, flags);
+
+	/*
+	 * No local open (never opened, or already closed and acked, e.g. when
+	 * qcom_glink_rx_close_ack() removes the rpmsg device and the core
+	 * destroys rpdev->ept): there is nothing to close, and a close for
+	 * lcid 0 only earns an ack for an unknown channel.
+	 */
+	if (!channel->lcid)
+		return;
 
 	qcom_glink_send_close_req(glink, channel);
 }
@@ -1754,8 +1774,10 @@
 		return;
 	}
 
-	idr_remove(&glink->lcids, channel->lcid);
-	channel->lcid = 0;
+	/* Remove the id that was acked, which is not always channel->lcid */
+	idr_remove(&glink->lcids, lcid);
+	if (channel->lcid == lcid)
+		channel->lcid = 0;
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&glink->idr_lock, flags);
 
 	/* Decouple the potential rpdev from the channel */
